hey guys we just watched the latest  trailer for Pokemon detective Pikachu  and just like many fans we're cautiously  optimistic we thought it would be fun to  compare this new film to the original  anime fans have been quick to point out  a few pretty major differences between  the two here's what we know about the  movie so far Harry  faked somebody else's death that last  one doesn't work Pokemon detective  Pikachu is a story that begins with a  missing persons case private  investigator Harry Goodman mysteriously  goes missing  Harry's 21 year old son Tim decides to  look for his dad and find out what  happened on his quest to find his father  Tim acquires an unlikely partner  detective Pikachu this little yellow  spark plug is a wisecracking gumshoe who  normally can't communicate with humans  it seems that Tim is the only human who  can understand him this unlikely duo  joins forces to solve the mystery of the  missing pie they sniff out clues through  the neon-lit streets of rhyme city an  electric modern metropolis where humans  and pokémon coexist they come across  various different Pokemon characters and  uncover an astonishing plot that puts  the future of the whole Pokemon universe  in jeopardy sounds pretty exciting right  Pokemon fans are holding their breath to  see if this film honors the characters  they know and love or if it's doomed to  be a disaster there are some notable  differences between the upcoming  live-action in the anime cartoon that  started in the late 90s for one the  beloved character Ash Ketchum is not  going to be in the film this surprised  fans because Ash has been the face of  the series for over two decades he's the  star of many animated features but  Pokemon detective Pikachu was from a  franchise spin-off game in the game  players solve mysteries with a talking  Pikachu this seems like an interesting  premise for a live-action film with CGI  animated characters but why no ash film  director rob letterman commented on the  decision saying that the Pokemon company  has already made many many movies with  ash the company came to legendary  entertainment with the idea of using a  new character Rob said that when he was  pitched the character detective Pikachu  he fell in love with the story behind  the character he said the story was  something with a lot of  heart and that it was very unique Rob  added that because there's already been  so much work done with ash he thought it  was a really good idea to try something  new with a different character for the  first live-action movie he did say that  he still wanted to base it in the  Pokemon universe meaning it still  follows all the rules that means we get  to see a lot of our favorite things from  the Polka verse Rob's not wrong about  how often Ash's story has been told so  doing a film without him might be a  refreshing change for Pokemon fans and  there are a lot of other characters to  choose from  so hopefully this film will convey the  heart of the story that Rob fell in love  with  even without ash these are just choices  another round extra shot another thing  that has fans cautiously curious is the  fact that Pikachu talks in the film  previously our beloved character could  only say pika Pikachu but the new  trailers clearly demonstrate that his  vocabulary has expanded quite a bit and  not only does he talk but he also has  the voice of Ryan Reynolds  that means Pikachu shares a voice with  Deadpool that makes for a pretty  interesting mesh of worlds apparently  before Ryan Reynolds was cast to voice  the new role there were rumors  circulating that a few other celebs were  being considered to play Pikachu  namely Danny DeVito and the rock but  according to director Rob Letterman  run-outs had a special quality that made  him perfect to play this little yellow  guy Letterman said there was something  delightful about Ryan's big personality  and voice and he liked the idea of  containing it all in this small package  he added that while it sounds like a  mismatch it's really organic and  downright hilarious another way that the  detective Pikachu movie is different  from the original anime cartoon is the  live-action CGI animation combo in the  original cartoon there's a distinct  style with which everyone is very  familiar and comfortable ash is a human  kid but is still drawn as a cartoon the  film takes a big leap from that universe  where actual humans are interacting with  Pokemon characters Rob Letterman said  that the Pokemon characters are  incredibly real and similar to Marvel's  guardians of the galaxy character Rocket  Raccoon it's as if he is real  their letterman boasts that the effects  in detective pikachu are some of the  most high-end visual effects in the  world he added that the film is  completely photorealistic causing  viewers to believe that though pokemons  are alive and in the movie there are  mixed feelings about this photo  realistic spin on the fan favorite  characters from the cartoons an article  in The Guardian said that the  natural-looking fur and skin on the  Pokemon characters is really creeping  people out the article said not only is  Pikachu hairy but Charizard is a scaly  dragon and mr. mime who was already the  stuff of nightmares now has a weird  plasticky face on top of that they said  that Jigglypuff looks like a fuzz ball  with a curl of human looking hair  another notable difference between the  Pokemon characters and detective Pikachu  is that the film is taking a bit of a  departure from the franchise and opting  to stick with the plotline from the  detective game that means Pokemon  characters will be doing a whole lot  more than the whole battle and capture  stuff from the trailer we can see that  detective Pikachu is going to have to  rely on his keen eye in cleverness  rather than his battle skills let's just  say that fans are approaching this new  film with cautious optimism so what do  you guys think about this upcoming movie  sound off in the comments section below  give this video a big thumbs up if  you're excited to watch detective  Pikachu and be sure to subscribe and hit  that notification bell to stay in the  loop thanks for watching the thing and  catch you next time  [Music]
 

